            Convergence round done (6c729dbf red checks, bf18e67f design): each lane record and owed row kind is one
            tagged Schema that the writer encodes with and the boot decodes with, so a decode accepts only what an
            encode produces (@spec.WriteAhead.R5, @spec.Codec.R5).

            Shapes the writers produce (read from lane-moves.ts, lanes.ts, ledger.ts, persist.ts, record.ts): actor
            record 1; lane `Head` (Held or in flight) and `Displaced`; owed rows `Answered` (on its lane, success,
            failure or unknown, value optional: answers, cancels, disposals, Restored, unsaved), `Unsent` (on its lane,
            a NotSent why), `Refused` (HoldRefused: operation and Attempt, no lane), `Declined` (operation and why). A
            kind stores nothing it determines (Refused's channel, a NotSent's `{ why }`).

