        comment     2026-11-19T07:50:41Z
            Second close review (fix round `70ca4def..4cd855c1`): ISSUES (independent lead, 2026-11-19). Three blocking
            findings; the first two have the same root cause as the previous blocker: a cleanup failure that never
            reaches the rejection. Gates, each alone: suite exit 1 (1279 passed, 25 expected fail, 1364 unhandled
            errors), `nub run check` exit 0, stress exit 0 (34 files), `nub run faults --only` 9 of 9 new faults caught.

            Blocking:
            1. Same root cause as before: a fiber's interrupt cleanup that fails with a typed error at the close is
               reported as success. `cleanupDied` in code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/driver.ts#makeDriver checks
               for a defect only, but Effect's `onInterrupt` and `onExit` cleanups can fail with a typed error, so the
               Exit holds an Interrupt and a Fail. Replayed as plain host tests: a store write whose cleanup fails
               `StoreRefused`, a runPromise Effect, and a read each leave `dispose()` with a success. That breaks
               @plan.Runtime.O6 ("never reported as success") and R23. Missing: a typed cleanup failure at the close for
               each kind of fiber, with a fault. Suggested fix: any Exit of a fiber the close interrupted that is more
               than an Interrupt counts as a failed cleanup.
            2. When the signal aborts a runPromise, the Effect's own cleanup failure is lost. `Fiber.interrupt` in
               code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/run-promise.ts#makeRunPromise throws away the inner fiber's Exit, so
               the rejection is RunFailed with only an Interrupt. The defect also goes nowhere else, since the life is
               still Open. Replayed: an abort whose cleanup dies gives a Cause without that defect. That breaks Q7 A
               ("the whole Cause") and acceptance item 5. Missing: an abort test whose cleanup dies or fails.
            3. The suite gate is red: `nub run test` exits 1. code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/surface/surface.test.ts
               throws hostile values at every entry, and each runPromise call returns a Promise that rejects RunFailed
               (for example "Not a valid effect: null") and is never handled. Deterministic, alone too. Missing: the
               walker settles a returned Promise; and a decision on whether runPromise refuses a value that is not an
               Effect at the boundary (@spec.Diagnostics R1).

            Asked checks:
            - The bound holds. A fully hung close can take three bounds (core, then fibers, then services), plus an
              unbounded forget. O6 and R23 bound the writes "from the call to dispose", and those all settle within the
              core's first bound. The two later stages decide no ending, and an overdue stage is CleanupOverdue, so no
              ending is lost. The catch is a stage that finishes after its bound: any Cause it adds after the snapshot
              is dropped, though dispose still rejects.
            - The quarantine lift is a reasonable reading of "until a cancel", but it is proposed and needs the user. An
              owner's cancel is a machine action and needs a live incarnation, which a quarantined ref can't get, so a
              literal cancel could never lift it. Trace 1: disposeActor with a read out, its cleanup dies, every ensure
              throws CleanupFailed with the Cause, a second disposeActor lifts it, and the next ensure starts fresh.
              Trace 2: disposeActor with a read out and its cleanup dies, then no ensure; a second disposeActor or
              `dispose()` succeeds, and the Cause is reported nowhere (no Issue, not in CleanupFailed). Replayed for
              `dispose()`. A restart drops it too, since the quarantine is in memory.
            - runPromise passes apart from 2 and 3: it refuses RuntimeNotReady and RuntimeDisposed with nothing run, a
              failure is RunFailed with the whole Cause, and disposal interrupts it. Typing is `Runtime<R>` with a
              method `runPromise`. A signal that is already aborted still runs the Effect's synchronous start, as
              `Effect.runPromise` does.
            - I30 catches both earlier classes (a Sent, and a Request after a Turn of the disposing open) and hides
              nothing. It over-flags two cases: a cleanup request from an interrupted read before RuntimeDisposed, and
              one after any Turn during the wait.
            - `Fiber.join` is right: every joiner gets the one Exit, and an interrupted caller only removes its
              own observer.

            Routed, not blocking (proposed owners; the orchestrator decides):
            - An unreported quarantine lost at `dispose()`, disposeActor or a restart (trace 2): the user, with the
              lift. The same goes for local actors' reads (no ensure can name `~N`) and for whether a grace end
              quarantines (it shares `retire`). Neither was replayed.
            - A `dispose({ forget: true })` whose caller is interrupted skips the forget, since the forget runs in the
              caller's fiber (pre-existing). `runPromise(runtime.dispose(...))` interrupts itself and skips the forget
              (not replayed). @task.V3.T100.
            - Overdue stages: a Cause added late is dropped, and services are released under fibers still
              running. @task.V3.T100.
            - The read quarantine checks for a defect only, so a read body that dies after its Interrupt is quarantined
              too. The per-read state is spread over `reading`, `endedReads` and `quarantined`, an implicit state
              machine against AGENTS.md. The `call` and Lookup observers repeat each other, and the comment on a read's
              "own wrapper" names nothing that exists. T99's fix round.
            - Stale text: the Life table's Run row still says its Booting cell waits on the user. `runtime-life.test.ts`
              cites R18 for a dependency rule. T99's fix round.

            Sidecars (6 Haiku, effort high), each finding verified:
            - Blind (O6, Q7, Q8, Actors, code): accepted the typed cleanup (blocking 1, replayed). Changed the
              quarantine at disposal into trace 2 (replayed). Routed the interrupted forget and the superseded read (an
              Open-life cleanup). Rejected the Booting ready hang (already routed) and the hang on an uninterruptible
              runPromise (the user's Effect, `Effect.runPromise` semantics). Noted the aborted-signal prefix.
            - Fiber kinds: accepted the defect-only check (1). Rejected "a dying cleanup loses its Interrupt": a probe
              on Effect 4.1.4 shows onInterrupt, onExit, ensuring and acquireRelease keep it; only a race, a timeout or
              a scoped child drop the defect entirely, which is @task.V3.T100's class.
            - Bound and quarantine: accepted the three-bound fact and judged it within O6. Accepted late Causes and
              trace 2. Rejected the ensure-after-lift race, which is a tested behaviour. The in-flight ticketless
              capture at the end of disposal was not verified: @task.V3.T100 to check.
            - runPromise: accepted the abort Cause loss (2, replayed). Verified the join semantics. Rejected the close
              fiber parked at construct (a Deferred wait, no work). Noted the bivariant method.
            - I30 and faults: accepted (above). All nine faults are real mutations caught for the stated reason.
            - Code quality: accepted the implicit read state, the repeated observers, the predicates, the test citation
              and the stale comment. Rejected "the Plan's public option" in suppressions as a temporary name: a Plan is
