        comment     2026-11-19T15:39:43Z
            Design (lead, proposed): one change per carrier, each a phantom or a parameter the producer already holds,
            carried across the seam to its consumer; the wide default stays assignable, so erased code (the core,
            generic rules, `(run: StoryRun)` helpers) keeps compiling. Gap numbers are the deep survey's (`g`), its
            entries and findings are the coverage pass's (`e`, `N`).

            The freedom it removes: a consumer may hold a narrow producer's value as `Values`, `string`, `never` or an
            erased carrier, so a typo, a foreign token or a wrong value compiles and reads undefined, matches nothing or
            faults late.

            F9 first, settled: `updateMemory` returning `{ notes, ticketId: "T-99" }` rewrites the `Flow.input` field at
            run time, and an undeclared key enters memory (red:
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/actors/memory-writes.test.ts). Two fixes: the turn refuses a patch naming
            a key outside the writable fields (InvalidTurn, refused whole, Turn R8), and the types refuse it first.

            Carriers (each probed in the scratchpad on a copy of `src/`: wrong lines fail for the stated reason, exact
            positives pass, `.not.toBeAny/Never/Unknown` hold, and the copy's own errors are fixed or counted):

            1. F9 exact returns: `machine<D, B = unknown>`, the body returning `MachineBody<D> & B & ExactBody<B, …>`,
               which walks only Flow's body, state, handler, alternative, reaction and schedule keys and the
               `updateMemory` return. The constrained `const B extends MachineBody<D>` loses today's weak-type refusals,
               so it is not used. Also exact: app entries; `runtimeSetup` takes `scope` and `persistence` together or
               neither; an empty payload takes no fields; `services` equals the commit's `R`; a widened `states` list is
               refused at `definition`; cheap construction refusals (duplicate state, empty compound, empty id) become
               types; `Fake` `handle` and `apply` become properties (no method bivariance). Closes g1-3, g32-34, e2,
               e11, e14, e15, N4, N6, part of e26. Fixtures 0 errors; tests 21 (2 intended, 10 directives to move, 4
               need a distributive `read`).
            2. F1 contract: `Bound` gains `~input`, `~key`, `~success`, `~failure` beside `~requires`; `const Key`
               limited to the input's required fields; handles take `BoundInput`/`BoundKey`; `SelectArg<M, P>` carries
               the handler's event, so `ActionToken<P>`/`GuardToken<P>`; `Attempt<I, K>`; `Snapshot.operations` keyed by
               operation name; `ContextSlot<V, P>` with `P` the provider's states and memory, and wiring typed by it on
               `actorRef` and `app` inputs. Closes g10, e3, e23 (input, key), seam 1 and 5, T104 items 1 and 3. Fixtures
               0 errors; one test needs `@ts-expect-error` (`KeyFieldOptional`).
            3. F5 snapshot view: `Snapshot<D, View = "inside">`; a handle's `getSnapshot()` is the outside view
               (`OutsideOf`, no `Flow.private` field); `context: Partial<ContextOf<…>>`; one exported `Lifecycle`; wide
               detection by the leaf union, not `AnyDefinition extends D` (contravariant, so `Snapshot<D>` would not
               assign to `Snapshot`). An `Unreadable { state, lifecycle, issues }` variant with no memory replaces the
               made-up `memory: {}` in `snapshotIn` and the stopped-Runtime `read`. Closes g19-21, e10, seam 7 and 8,
               T103's routed item 1.
            4. F4 app: `RuntimeSetup<R, A>` and `Runtime<R, A>` carry `~app`; `Story<Names, Ds>`, `StoryRun<Names, Ds>`,
               `Cut<Ds>`, `Recorded<Ds>`; every ref word takes `D extends Ds`; selectors take only `Ds` tokens;
               `publishedOf<D extends Ds, Ds>` (that order keeps `typeof publishedOf<X>`). With `Steps<Names>` and the
               default `StoryRun<never>`, checkpoint names survive `run({ steps })` and helpers take `<N>(run:
               StoryRun<N>)`. Closes g14-18, e1, e19, N3, the F3/F4 selector extension, T103's routed item 3. Wide types
               still assign to their defaults.
            5. F6 with F8: `Evidence<N extends Names = WideNames>`; tokens carry `~names`, and the selectors return rows
               narrowed to the definition's states, events and operations. Closed vocabularies by existing unions:
               `RuntimeCut` rows from `Phase["_tag"]`, `Channel`, `Delivery["_tag"]`, the timer kind; `SlowWork.input`
               as `Input["_tag"]`; `decline` and `notSent` take `Decline` and `NotSentWhy`; `Diagnostic` as a union by
               code, each with the detail keys Flow writes; `Tab.name: "main"`; `Property<R>`/`Failure<R>`; bench `kind:
               Measure` and `bench<const C>` with `` id: `${NoInfer<C>}.${string}` ``; `Channel`, `LaneFact`,
