              (`host/driver.ts:217`); one contract may be bound under several names.
            - Record keys at `Fake.storage.put` and `Cut.records.stored` (e8, part of seam 12): @spec.Stories R11 keeps
              put's keys raw, since the records it stands for are the ones no key builder makes.
            - `Unsettled.state` (part of g28): already `"InFlight" | "Held"`. Operations-record excess keys and nested
              `states` keys: already refused.

            Limits, each recorded (TypeScript, not a choice):

            - A brand is a subtype of `string`, so `attempt === someText` still compiles; only parameters and
              brand-to-brand compares refuse.
            - `onContext` as an array literal cannot infer a reaction's value from its `select`, so g9 and N7 stay open
              there. A curried `react(select)(event, when?)` infers both (probed): a new public shape, for the
              user's decision.
            - A computed `Flow.initial(schema, (fields) => …)` cannot see its siblings' types (N2): the inner call
              resolves before `definition` has `M`. Closing it needs a new shape (memory as a callback, or a builder),
              for the user's decision.
            - `Ended.reason` stays `string` on the row: it mixes the contract's own failure tags with Flow's `Decline`;
              a `TaggedEnum` variant cannot hold the correlated union. Flow's own writes are typed at `decline`
              and `notSent`.
            - `Cut.calls` stays the wide log generic rules read; a typed read is `read(endpoint)`, so the literal
              compares in tests move there.
            - `Step.checkpoint({ name })` stays text; a negative `captureMs` is a run-time refusal.

            New public type parameters and names (delegated; for the user's read): `ContextSlot<V, P>`, `RuntimeSetup<R,
            A>`, `Runtime<R, A>`, `Snapshot<D, View>`, `Story<Names, Ds>`, `StoryRun<Names, Ds>` (default
            `StoryRun<never>`), `Cut<Ds>`, `Recorded<Ds>`, `Steps<Names>`, `Ending<V>`, `UnknownEnding`,
            `WriteEndings<E, A>`, `ReadEndings<E, A>`, `Attempt<I, K>`, `Evidence<N>`, `Property<R>`, `Failure<R>`, the
            token brands, `Lifecycle`, `Unreadable`, and the exported `Channel`, `LaneFact`, `ReportCode`, `Phase`.
            Public shape changes: `getSnapshot()` may return `Unreadable`; `Fake` handlers as properties; `services`
            must equal `R`; `scope` and `persistence` together.
